@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title The six migration phases and what each one needs before it can start

start

:**Phase 0 — the conformance gate**
Measure the twelve cells: three capabilities
by search, vocabulary, detail, selection.
For each cell report whether a tool class exists,
whether anything dispatches it, and where its
routes live. Today that reads 6 live, 2 declared
and dead, 1 borrowed, 3 absent;
note right
  Built first because it is the only thing that
  can say a later phase finished. Without a number
  that moves, "the routes were moved" is a claim
  nobody can check afterwards.
end note

fork
  :**Phase 1 — the tool contract in the library**
  One shape every capability tool satisfies, so
  search, vocabulary, detail and selection mean
  the same thing in all three capabilities.
  ChatHealthyTool and the unsubclassed
  CapabilitySearchTool are what exists to build on;
fork again
  :**Phase 2 — split app.py by capability**
  The 14 routes in
  Code/ConversationalUX/FindCareChat/backend/app.py
  leave for the FindCare/ feature directory that
  already holds their service;
end fork

:**Phase 3 — the router dispatches tools**
The three inline branches — specialtySearch,
findAFacility, findAProvider — stop building
httpx calls and stream events and call a tool
by name. FacilitySearchTool already holds the
work findAFacility duplicates;
note right
  Needs Phase 1 for the contract to dispatch
  against, and Phase 2 so the route the tool
  reaches is at its final address.
end note

:**Phase 4 — fill the missing tools**
facility vocabulary, trial vocabulary and
trial detail do not exist. Facility detail is
served by ProviderDetailTool with entity_type=2
and gets its own tool or a stated decision
that sharing one is correct;

:**Phase 5 — retire the rest of Code/**
Frontend shell, the iPhone tests, the
about-content files, Code/Shared and
Code/Shared/ops. Then the six build-tooling
paths change and the tree is deleted;

stop

floating note left
  Phase 0 is not a step in this sequence so much as
  the instrument the sequence is read with. Every
  phase below it ends by the gate reporting a
  different number, and a phase that moves no number
  did not do what it said.
end note

@enduml
